        </pattern>
        <rect width="100%" height="100%" fill="url(#dot-pattern-reebokfr20zfloatridetreadmill)"></rect>
      </svg>
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 relative z-10 text-center">
        <div class="flex justify-center mb-6">
          <TrustBadge />
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-3 mb-6 flex-wrap">
          <span class="bg-[#FF5A1F] text-white px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">
            Model Review
          </span>
          <span class="bg-green-500 text-white px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">
            Updated October 2026
          </span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black text-white leading-tight mb-8">
          Reebok FR20z Floatride <span class="text-[#5AA9FF]">Treadmill Review</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
          The FR20z is a compact, fixed-deck treadmill built around Reebok’s Floatride cushioning, with power incline and Zwift support. It is a sensible machine for walkers and steady runners — and, for American buyers, a hard one to find new, because it is sold mainly in the UK, Europe and Australia.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
          <a href="#where-it-is-sold" class="bg-[#FF5A1F] hover:bg-[#E64F16] text-white px-8 py-4 rounded-xl font-black no-underline transition-colors uppercase tracking-widest text-sm">
            Where It Is Sold
          </a>
          <a href="#specifications" class="bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 text-white px-8 py-4 rounded-xl font-black no-underline transition-colors uppercase tracking-widest text-sm border border-white/20">
            The Specifications
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>


    <!-- Author & Meta -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-12">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 py-8 border-b border-gray-100">
        <img src="https://i.pravatar.cc/150?img=48" alt="Morgan Reyes" class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full" />
        <div>
          <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 leading-tight">Morgan Reyes</p>
          <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm leading-tight">Fitness Equipment Editor</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block w-px h-8 bg-gray-200"></div>
        <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm">
          Last Updated: <strong class="text-gray-700">October 14, 2026</strong>
        </p>
        <div class="ml-auto">
          <SocialProof users="1.6k" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="not-prose my-10 bg-blue-50 border border-blue-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 m-0 leading-relaxed">
          <strong class="text-gray-900">What we checked, and what we have not done.</strong> On
          14 October 2026 we checked the FR20z on Reebok Fitness's official UK and Australian
          stores, Reebok's US fitness store, the listing of Lifespan Fitness (an Australian
          retailer that stocks the Reebok range), Amazon's US listings, and independent reviews
          from Home Treadmill (updated August 2026) and Gym Tech Review (December 2024), with other
          UK reviews for context. The figures on this page are those on which the official listings
          and at least one independent source agree. Where they disagree — the warranty, the
          number of programmes, whether the incline levels are percentages, a continuous motor
          rating — we say so rather than choose. We have not tested the FR20z; nothing here is our
          own measurement. Prices are those shown on the dates stated and change often.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
      <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
        <h2 class="flex items-center gap-2 text-lg font-black text-gray-900 mt-0 mb-4">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5 text-[#FF5A1F]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4 6h16M4 12h16M4 18h7"></path></svg>
          In This Guide
        </h2>
        <nav class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2">
          <a href="#short-answer" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">1. The Reebok FR20z Floatride Treadmill: The Short Answer</a>
          <a href="#where-it-is-sold" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">2. Where the Reebok FR20z Is Sold, and the US Problem</a>
          <a href="#specifications" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">3. The Reebok FR20z Specifications, Agreed and Disputed</a>
          <a href="#motor-and-speed" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">4. The Motor and the 11.2 mph Ceiling</a>
          <a href="#deck-and-cushioning" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">5. The Deck and the Floatride Cushioning</a>
          <a href="#incline-console-apps" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">6. Incline, Console, Programmes and Apps</a>
          <a href="#what-reviewers-report" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">7. What Independent Reviewers Consistently Report</a>
          <a href="#warranty-and-delivery" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">8. Warranty, Delivery and Space</a>
          <a href="#alternatives" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">9. Alternatives on This Site, Especially for US Buyers</a>
          <a href="#verdict" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">10. The Verdict</a>
          <a href="#faq" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">11. Frequently Asked Questions</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          The Reebok FR20z Floatride treadmill gets a lot of searches for a machine most American
          shoppers cannot easily buy. It is a real, current product with official Reebok Fitness
          stores in the UK and Australia and listings across Europe and the Middle East. In the
          US the picture is thinner: Reebok's own US fitness store listed no treadmills at all when
          we checked, and the FR20z listings we found on Amazon's US site were marked currently
          unavailable. This review sets out what the FR20z is, which figures the official listings
          and independent reviewers agree on, where the sources conflict, and what to do if you are
          in the US and want one.
        </p>

        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">1. The Reebok FR20z Floatride Treadmill: The Short Answer</h2>
<p>
            <strong>The Reebok FR20z Floatride treadmill is a compact, non-folding home treadmill
            with cushioned decking, power incline and Zwift support, and it is sold mainly outside
            the US.</strong> In the UK, Europe and Australia it is a reasonable mid-range machine
            for walking, incline walking and steady running. Its official listings and independent
            reviewers agree on the core figures: a 140 by 46 cm deck, a 2.25 HP peak motor, 18 km/h
            (11.2 mph), 15 incline levels and a 120 kg (264 lb) user limit.
          </p>
          <p>
            Two things hold it back. The first is the deck: 46 cm is about 18 inches wide and 140 cm
            is about 55 inches long, which suits walkers and runners of average height at moderate
            pace but leaves little margin for tall or fast runners. The second, for American
            readers, is availability. Reebok's US fitness store listed no treadmills when we
            checked on 14 October 2026, its FR20z product page there no longer loads, and the FR20z
            listings on Amazon's US site were marked currently unavailable. A machine you cannot
            easily buy, have serviced or claim warranty on locally is a weaker proposition than the
            same machine in a market where it is stocked.
          </p>
          <p>
            So the answer depends on where you live. In the UK or Australia, the FR20z is worth
            shortlisting if you walk or run steadily, value cushioning and have room for a
            treadmill that stays up. In the US, look at machines with local stock and support first
            — we suggest some in the alternatives section — and buy an FR20z only from a seller
            who can show it is a US-voltage unit with a warranty honoured in the US. We have not
            tested the FR20z; everything below is from published listings and independent reviews.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Product cards -->
      <div class="not-prose">
        {
          PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => (
            <div id={product.id} class="scroll-mt-24 mt-12 first:mt-8">
              <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-sm">
                <div class="bg-gray-900 px-6 py-4 flex items-center justify-between flex-wrap gap-3">
